Done — I set the print up for strength and started slicing. What I changed:

- **Walls: 2 → 4 loops.** On a flat 5–7 mm plaque, the walls are what takes the load, so this is the single biggest gain.
- **Infill: 15% crosshatch → 40% gyroid.** Gyroid is stiff in every direction, not just along the grid lines.
- **Bottom solid layers: 3 → 4**, matching the 5-layer top so the part resists bending from both faces.
- **Layer height kept at 0.20 mm** — thinner layers mostly add print time here.

Slicing is running now; you can watch it in the card below, with a Cancel button if you change your mind. When it finishes I'll read what the slice says — print time, filament use and any warnings — and tell you if anything looks off before you send it to the printer.

Two things I'm taking on trust: that the spool in the printer really is the Bambu PLA Basic the project has picked, and that the arrow and the two arcs are meant to print together as one design rather than as separate pieces (they overlap on the plate).
